#h1{Appendix: the plain parts}

The entry point, argument handling, text comparison, the module file and the assets of the woven
page. Each is what its name says.

#lit: the command's main{
  The program is one binary, and `main` does nothing but hand the arguments and the three streams
  to the library, so tests can run the same commands in memory.

  ```
  // Command lit is the brashtag literate-programming toolkit: tangle, weave, absorb, sync and the rest, in one binary.
  package main

  import (
  	"os"

  	"github.com/pratikdeoghare/brashtag-literate/internal/lit"
  )

  func main() {
  	os.Exit(lit.Main(os.Args[1:], lit.IO{In: os.Stdin, Out: os.Stdout, Err: os.Stderr, IsTTY: lit.IsTerminal(os.Stdin)}))
  }
  ```
}

